<title>FRANCE: AGF shares slump on interest in GAN.</title>
<headline>AGF shares slump on interest in GAN.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Assurances Generales de France (AGF) fell sharply on Friday after the group expressed interest in bidding for state insurer GAN, slated for privatisation.</p>
<p>AGF chairman Antoine Jeancourt-Galignani said on Thursday, &quot;We are observing the situation...We have to know how, when and under what conditions it (the government) plans to privatise it.&quot; He said GAN had activities that &quot;complement our own&quot;.</p>
<p>AGF shares were down 5.36 percent at 203 francs, the biggest fall on the CAC index, which was down 1.7 percent at 1015 GMT.</p>
<p>Dupont Denant lowered its recommendation on the AGF share to hold from buy, citing the prospect of AGF acquisitions in the aftermath of the Axa-UAP megamerger.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
